  *
  * Auto focus
  *
- * Contrast detection autofocus on the software ISP's focus measure (the
- * absolute second derivative of green in the centre of the image, divided
- * by the green level so that exposure changes do not count as focus
- * changes). A scan visits the lens range in coarse steps, then the
- * neighbourhood of the best coarse position (see below), waiting a few
- * statistics periods after every lens move (the statistics are gathered on
- * every fourth frame, which is enough for a voice coil lens to settle). In continuous mode a scan is started at
- * the beginning and again when the measure at the chosen position changes
- * for several frames (scene change). Lens positions are on a 0..100 scale
- * mapped linearly onto the lens driver's focus range.
+ * Contrast detection autofocus on the software ISP's focus measure: the
+ * absolute second derivative of green in the focus window, divided by the
+ * green level of the same samples so that neither the exposure nor the rest
+ * of the image count as focus changes. Lens positions are on a 0..100 scale
+ * mapped linearly onto the lens driver's focus range (0 = infinity end).
  *
- * Faster scans (diting): the coarse pass stops as soon as the measure has
- * fallen well below its peak for a few steps (the peak has been passed),
- * the fine pass only covers +-fineRange around the coarse peak, the lens
- * range can be limited (rangeMin, rangeMax: positions the module can
- * focus at), and continuous mode waits for a larger and longer change
- * before rescanning.
+ * Two searches (diting):
  *
- * The fine pass only measures two positions, fineRange on either side of
- * the coarse peak, and the lens goes to the vertex of the parabola through
- * the best measure and its two neighbours (in position order, over both
- * passes): about half the measures of a fine grid, with a finer result.
+ * - Full scan, when nothing is known (first start, local search without a
+ *   result): the lens range in coarse steps, from the near end so that the
+ *   first peak met, where the scan stops, is the closest subject.
+ *
+ * - Local search, for every later refocus: the measure at the current
+ *   position, then on either side of it, further and further out (growing
+ *   steps, the rising side first) until the best measure has a clearly
+ *   lower one (climbMargin) on both sides. When the lens is still at the
+ *   peak that takes three measures and the image hardly moves.
+ *
+ * Both end with measures at fineRange on either side of the best one, the
+ * lens goes to the vertex of the parabola through the three, and the measure
+ * there is checked against the best one (the lens goes back to the best
+ * measured position if the fit was wrong).
+ *
+ * While a search runs the software ISP gathers the focus measure on every
+ * frame instead of every fourth, the AGC holds the exposure, and in low
+ * light (high gain) every position is measured more than once. A search
+ * during which the scene changes would mix measures of two scenes: it
+ * starts again when the brightness of the focus window jumps
+ * (sceneThreshold), and the measures the result rests on are taken again
+ * if they are old.
+ *
+ * Continuous mode refocuses when the measure at the chosen position has
+ * changed for a few statistics, but only once the scene and the exposure
+ * are steady again (no search while the phone is being moved), and not at
+ * all if the measure comes back to what it was. After a search without a
+ * result (no texture, too dark) the lens goes back to the last good
+ * position and the next search waits.
+ *
+ * The application can choose the subject: AfMetering = Windows and one
+ * AfWindows rectangle, in units of 1/10000 of the image as announced by the
+ * control's limits (the simple pipeline has no ScalerCropMaximum). A new
+ * window starts a full scan: the closest subject in it wins.
  */
 
